WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.020
Konino is one of the settlements with the funniest names in Serbia.

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.300
All of Serbia is full of villages with such silly and strange names.

3
00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:07.960
Mozgovo, Kurići.

4
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.020
And today we'll be doing exactly that.

5
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:13.940
We're visiting ten places with the strangest names and taking photos at every sign at the entrance.

6
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:20.720
We got up at six in the morning, filled up the tank and headed for the first village — only 30 km from our city.

7
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.220
Since it's David's idea, he's at the wheel.

8
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.400
But it's your video, you... [inaudible]

9
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:32.640
On a map of the whole of Serbia we chose ten places and plotted a route — roughly like this.

10
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.720
A little more and we're in Konino.

11
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.040
David!

12
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.220
Where's the road?

13
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:38.220
Where's the road?

14
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:42.860
This is Konino.

15
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.440
Now we stick on a sticker and take a photo at the sign.

16
00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:47.740
And where do we get stickers?

17
00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:49.840
Let's go back a week.

18
00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:56.780
Since we're driving around villages with funny names, I decided to put a sticker on each sign themed on the name.

19
00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:58.240
For that I need a designer.

20
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.860
But one who can stand in the "Triangle" forever.

21
00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.040
How long do you think you'll last in the "Triangle"?

22
00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.160
Forever, [inaudible].

23
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:05.240
Forever.

24
00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:09.580
This is Kepawoz, a YouTuber from Kruševac, who stood with me in the "Triangle" at Mario's.

25
00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:10.680
[inaudible]

26
00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:11.780
[inaudible]

27
00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.220
Oh, where are you, Kepa?

28
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.420
Oh, hi.

29
00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.000
Why are you dressed up like that, bro?

30
00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.740
Oh, bro, we've got all kinds of holidays here.

31
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.760
I told you I'd call today — I need your help.

32
00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.160
I'm filming a video.

33
00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:24.500
Oh, which one?

34
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:28.280
I want to tour the villages with the funniest names in Serbia.

35
00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.260
Bro, great.

36
00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:34.620
In every village I want to take a photo at the sign and stick a sticker on it.

37
00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.720
And I want to ask you to draw the sticker.

38
00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.280
Sure, it can be done.

39
00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.020
And which villages are we talking about?

40
00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:41.920
Well look: there's Konino...

41
00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.960
Kepa is a cool YouTuber with really awesome ideas.

42
00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:48.620
So I expect you to thank him for the stickers too and watch one of his videos.

43
00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.300
In all we have 10 stickers.

44
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.660
More precisely, already 9 — we've already been to Konino.

45
00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:56.680
The next village is 130 km away, we got there by 8 o'clock.

46
00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:01.350
The second village is Donje Brijane ("Lower Shaving").

47
00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:03.830
Well, here it's clear why the name is funny.

48
00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:06.290
We stick a sticker here too and take photos.

49
00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:12.730
David and I post the photo at each sign on Instagram — you can check it out right away and like it too.

50
00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:18.790
On the way to the next village we got hungry and stopped at the creepiest store we'd ever seen.

51
00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:24.110
But the saleswoman turned out to be so sweet and friendly that we immediately felt ashamed of such thoughts.

52
00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:25.110
Thank you, all the best.

53
00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:26.110
Thank you too.

54
00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:30.110
I walk into [inaudible]...

55
00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:33.430
[inaudible] pours from a two-liter bottle into a small one.

56
00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.370
Spilled everything.

57
00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.270
Spilled all the cola.

58
00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.730
We drove another 35 km to the next village.

59
00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:43.550
While I was looking for villages with the funniest names and plotting the route,

60
00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.350
I noticed that almost all of them are in the south of Serbia.

61
00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:47.910
And I realized we have a problem.

62
00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:49.610
Well, that is — Krastavče.

63
00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:53.850
Krastavče is the next village.

64
00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:55.850
And here we are at the sign at the entrance.

65
00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:59.990
Symbolic: in this village David and I will each eat a cucumber.

66
00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.060
Now we stick on the sticker and take photos.

67
00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:09.460
The next village is 50 km away, but we got there faster than we thought.

68
00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:16.060
We got here fast, and we're leaving even faster — we're in Smrdić.

69
00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.420
We stick on the sticker and go.

70
00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:21.660
David and I get up to such things even when we're not filming.

71
00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.420
It's never normal, and sometimes it's dangerous.

72
00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:32.770
So hit the red button if you haven't subscribed yet.

73
00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.190
So that we do even crazier things.

74
00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:38.650
While I was begging for subscriptions, we reached the next village — Selište.

75
00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:39.830
Where to now, David?

76
00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:40.450
Selište.

77
00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.930
We're going to Selište.

78
00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:45.760
Selište.

79
00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.780
The name, in fact, describes the place.

80
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.320
We barely made it here.

81
00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.920
Now we stick on the sticker and drive on.

82
00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:57.880
Selište is near Prokuplje, and Kepawoz struggled with it the most when coming up with the design.

83
00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:00.200
Well, how do you draw "Selište"?

84
00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:04.540
But he showed talent and pulled through — the sticker turned out very creative.

85
00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.560
By the way, later we pass through Kruševac.

86
00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:10.340
We have skateboards in the car, and Kruševac has a great skate park.

87
00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:13.060
And we can also invite Kepa to hang out with us.

88
00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:15.440
By the way, on the way to Selište the car overheated a bit.

89
00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:19.320
The water in the radiator began to boil, so it's good that we made it out.

90
00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:20.820
We're approaching the sixth village.

91
00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.340
The sixth village is Dupci, or, simply put, "butts."

92
00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.740
But how could it go without complications.

93
00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:29.980
Google Maps led us another way — uphill, to the center of the village.

94
00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.920
We began climbing to where Dupci is.

95
00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.160
But there's no sign and no road.

96
00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.760
Let's see if there's a turn signpost for Dupci somewhere — we'll take a photo at that at least.

97
00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.840
Never mind, guys, now we're by the lake in a place called Zlatari.

98
00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:44.660
And here to the left is the turn to the village of Dupci.

99
00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:49.640
We drove up and saw that the road is like this and there's no sign.

100
00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:55.760
So this beautifully drawn sticker with butts, unfortunately, won't be stuck anywhere.

101
00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.700
Although this whole area belongs to the village of Dupci.

102
00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:03.060
If we'd taken any other main road, we'd have come across the "Dupci" sign.

103
00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.820
Anyway, we gave up and drove to the next village.

104
00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:09.500
But the road to the next village was wider, and this is what happened.

105
00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:12.400
We're going to Brus, and over there is some yellow sign.

106
00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.200
To D...

107
00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:18.610
We found Dupci!

108
00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.000
The sixth village — Dupci.

109
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.340
I can only imagine how this village got its name.

110
00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:29.240
And again a brilliant illustration: butts, little butts, rear ends.

111
00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:32.340
Again we stick on the sticker and take photos at the sign.

112
00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:33.960
And drive on.

113
00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.900
This time not a village but a little town — Brus.

114
00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:43.760
We know Bruce Willis, Bruce Lee — and this is our Serbian Brus.

115
00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:47.000
True, borrowed from the Germanism Büstenhalter (brassiere), but ours.

116
00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:50.220
There's a charming politician here who adores March 8.

117
00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.800
Oh, I got a text message.

118
00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:55.260
Here we stick on the sticker and get out of here right away.

119
00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:57.560
Phew, we escaped from Brus.

120
00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:58.680
Sounds strange.

121
00:05:58.680 --> 00:05:59.900
We're already a bit tired.

122
00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:03.660
We still have three places to visit, and we'll also stop at the skate park in Kruševac.

123
00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:06.920
To get to the next village we need to go around Kopaonik.

124
00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:09.720
The road was so-so, and almost all the time uphill.

125
00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:13.140
And when the car overheated again, I stopped to take a few shots with the drone.

126
00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:16.840
And completely by chance I filmed one of the most beautiful fortresses in Serbia.

127
00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.560
The medieval town of Koznik.

128
00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:21.880
Only on the way back did I realize we had driven past it.

129
00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.180
There was no time now — we're driving on.

130
00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:28.360
And so, after an hour and a half on the road, we finally reached Kurići.

131
00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.660
Yes, the next village is Kurići.

132
00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:33.680
If I laughed at this name — I should go back to first grade.

133
00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:36.760
When we reached Kurići, which are definitely on Google Maps,

134
00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:40.140
it turned out to be part of a village.

135
00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:41.620
Not even a village.

136
00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:46.340
The eighth village — Kurići.

137
00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:47.900
But there's no sign.

138
00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:51.420
It's called Kurići, Kurići exist, but there's no sign.

139
00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:53.620
Why did we lose three hours?

140
00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:59.220
Guys, Kurići is just a hamlet, some mahala next to the village of Korlače.

141
00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:03.000
Korlače. Since there's nowhere to stick the sticker — there's no "Kurići" signpost,

142
00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:06.100
there's a sign for the neighboring village of Piskane,

143
00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:09.040
which vandals altered to read "Piškane."

144
00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:13.160
So we've connected Kurići with Piškane — that's where we'll stick it.

145
00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:15.520
Now we're going back about three kilometers down.

146
00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:24.180
And while we're still alive — we stick the "Kurići" sticker on the "Piškane" signpost.

147
00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:27.580
That is, "Piskane," but here it is — the "Kurići" sticker.

148
00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:29.920
And here are the photos at the "Piškane" sign.

149
00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:32.220
We drove on, ready to skate in Kruševac.

150
00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:35.900
But the road from Kurići to Kruševac took two and a half hours.

151
00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:38.180
Well, that's how long it took for Milan, who was driving.

152
00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:39.540
David and I slept through all of it.

153
00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.120
Only two villages left.

154
00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:43.820
When we finally arrived in Kruševac, it was already dark.

155
00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:45.840
And where did we arrive? We arrived in...

156
00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:46.840
Kruševac!

157
00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:53.360
But it's already getting dark, so the remaining two villages we'll apparently film in the dark.

158
00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.880
But Kepawoz was waiting for us at the skate park.

159
00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:58.000
The man thanks to whom we have all these stickers.

160
00:07:58.200 --> 00:07:59.360
Oh, good evening, colleague.

161
00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:00.880
Good evening, colleague, how are you?

162
00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:01.920
Fine, and you?

163
00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:03.780
Not bad, we came to skate.

164
00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:06.880
By the way, guys, this is the very guy who drew the stickers.

165
00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:10.720
Too bad I've used them all up, or I'd show how the rest turned out.

166
00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:12.040
But that's how it is.

167
00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:13.760
And...

168
00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:15.120
[inaudible]

169
00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:17.320
[inaudible]

170
00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:19.020
That's all I can do...

171
00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:20.360
Will I be able to do it like that?

172
00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:22.300
Whoa!

173
00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:24.080
[inaudible]

174
00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.760
[inaudible]

175
00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:28.200
[inaudible]

176
00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:54.320
So, we met Kepa.

177
00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:57.220
Although I'd met him before in the "Triangle" at Mario's,

178
00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:00.800
I still needed to meet and thank him personally for the stickers.

179
00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:03.500
He really went to a lot of trouble — made them in literally two or three days.

180
00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.360
We wanted to reach the last village while it was still light,

181
00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.540
but that was impossible — it had already gotten dark.

182
00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:12.080
Good thing I brought this lamp in the back — it shines blue.

183
00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:14.060
The next village is Donji Ljubeš.

184
00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:16.180
Again a village with a dubious origin of its name.

185
00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.700
But we're slowly getting closer to the last village.

186
00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:23.100
Next in line is the village of Donji Ljubeš.

187
00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:25.480
Again a village with a name of dubious origin,

188
00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:27.380
but it's the second-to-last village.

189
00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:29.560
After it — the last one.

190
00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:32.000
Again we stick on the sticker and take photos at the sign,

191
00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.240
only now in the dark.

192
00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:36.060
David and I post all these photos on Instagram.

193
00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:37.240
So subscribe.

194
00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.240
There I post behind-the-scenes from filming in my stories

195
00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:41.500
and shots that I'm not allowed to put in the video.

196
00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.040
And — the moment of truth.

197
00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:45.120
The last village — Mozgovo.

198
00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.800
David, bro, just a little more.

199
00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:49.780
[inaudible] Mozgovo...

200
00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.320
A little more and we're at the last one.

201
00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:53.820
Another kilometer and a half.

202
00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.320
And then home.

203
00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:57.060
Oh, ready?

204
00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.580
Am I seeing this?

205
00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:02.210
Am I seeing this?

206
00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:04.610
Mozgovo!

207
00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:08.310
Hey, Mozgovo!

208
00:10:10.570 --> 00:10:13.030
[inaudible]

209
00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:17.840
Well, guys, we're at the last village,

210
00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.320
at the last sign, it's very cold.

211
00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:21.280
There isn't a single streetlight here.

212
00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.180
Standing here is a big risk.

213
00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.620
This is Mozgovo, the last village,

214
00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.900
and David and I belong right here, because

215
00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:29.200
we're smart.

216
00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:30.900
The last sticker, we need to hurry.

217
00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.680
Come on, faster, [inaudible].

218
00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.620
So, here it is — the "Mozgovo" sticker.

219
00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:35.580
Mozgovo!

220
00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:37.280
Drawn by Kepawoz, he says: "mine."

221
00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:39.400
We stick on the last sticker,

222
00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:41.500
take photos and head home.

223
00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:42.940
Mozgovo!

224
00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:46.560
Guys, huge thanks for being here and watching my videos.

225
00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:48.940
In the summer, of course, expect new episodes about camping.

226
00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:51.060
Or watch the previous ones if you haven't seen them yet.

227
00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:52.840
We're already planning a whole project.

228
00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:53.560
See you!